{
  "id": "Lyo.FileMetadataStore.Sqlite",
  "name": "Lyo.FileMetadataStore.Sqlite",
  "area": "Data",
  "tagline": "EF Core SQLite IFileMetadataStore. Same store and adjunct services as Lyo.FileMetadataStore.Postgres, for embedded, offline-first, and local-dev hosts.",
  "description": "EF Core SQLite IFileMetadataStore. Same store and adjunct services as [Lyo.FileMetadataStore.Postgres](../Lyo.FileMetadataStore.Postgres/README.md), for embedded, offline-first, and local-dev hosts.",
  "features": [],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Add the SQLite store",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "using Lyo.FileMetadataStore.Sqlite;\n\n// Simple\nservices.AddSqliteFileMetadataStore(\"Data Source=./filestore.db\");\n\n// With auto-migrations at host startup\nservices.AddSqliteFileMetadataStoreDbContextFactoryFromConfiguration(configuration);\nservices.AddSqliteFileMetadataStore();\nservices.AddSqliteFileAuditSink();\nservices.AddSqliteFileDownloadAccessService();\n\n// Keyed (multi-store hosts)\nservices.AddSqliteFileMetadataStoreKeyed(\"sqlite-metadata\")\n    .ConfigureSqliteFileStore(options => {\n        options.ConnectionString = \"Data Source=./filestore.db\";\n        options.EnableAutoMigrations = true;\n    })\n    .Build();"
    },
    {
      "title": "appsettings.json",
      "language": "json",
      "code": "{\n  \"SqliteFileMetadataStore\": {\n    \"ConnectionString\": \"Data Source=./filestore.db\",\n    \"EnableAutoMigrations\": true\n  }\n}"
    },
    {
      "title": "Attach to keyed file storage",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "services.AddS3FileStorageServiceKeyed(\"my-files\")\n    .UseFileMetadataStore(\"sqlite-metadata\")\n    .Build(configuration);"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Types",
      "headers": [
        "Component",
        "Role"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "SqliteFileMetadataStore",
          "IFileMetadataStore + IHealth"
        ],
        [
          "SqliteFileAuditSink",
          "IFileAuditEventHandler. Append-only audit rows."
        ],
        [
          "SqliteMultipartUploadSessionStore",
          "IMultipartUploadSessionStore"
        ],
        [
          "SqliteFileDownloadAccessService",
          "Time-limited download access tokens"
        ],
        [
          "SqliteFileMetadataStoreDbContext",
          "EF Core context (5 tables, same shape as Postgres)"
        ]
      ],
      "trail": "Tables: `file_metadata`, `file_data`, `file_audit_events`, `multipart_upload_session`, `file_download_access_links`."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "title": "How to register",
      "text": "`appsettings.json`: Point blob storage at the keyed metadata store the same way as Postgres:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "title": "How migrations run",
      "text": "Migrations ship in this package. Turn on EnableAutoMigrations (via [`Lyo.Sqlite`](../../Sqlite/Lyo.Sqlite/README.md)) or run `dotnet ef database update` using SqliteFileMetadataStoreDbContextFactory. Design-time connection string: FILEMETADATASTORE_CONNECTION_STRING or FILESTORE_CONNECTION_STRING (defaults to `Data Source=./filestore-design.db`). `DropStagedFileUpload` removes the former `staged_file_upload` table. `AddFileMetadataJson` adds opaque `metadata_json` on `file_metadata` and `multipart_upload_session`."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "title": "Writer limits",
      "text": "SQLite is single-writer. Fine for embedded clients, local tools, and low-concurrency dev hosts. High-throughput multi-instance ingestion should use Postgres. Enable WAL at the connection level if the host opens many concurrent readers (`PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL`)."
    }
  ],
